# `rules_haskell` Architecture

This documents the internal architecture of `rules_haskell` — a Bazel ruleset for
building Haskell code. It is intended for contributors and maintainers.

## Workspace Layout

Three Bazel workspaces form the repository:

| Workspace              | Purpose                                    |
|------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `/` (root)             | Core rule definitions and implementation   |
| `rules_haskell_tests/` | Comprehensive test suite (115+ test dirs)  |
| `rules_haskell_nix/`   | Nixpkgs integration and examples           |

## Layered Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Public API (haskell/defs.bzl)      │
│  haskell_library, haskell_binary,   │ ← macros/attrs users call
│  haskell_test, haskell_import,      │
│  haskell_repl, haskell_doc          │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Implementation                     │
│  haskell/private/haskell_impl.bzl   │ ← core logic per rule type
│  _haskell_binary_common_impl,       │
│  haskell_library_impl, etc.         │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Context                            │
│  haskell/private/context.bzl        │ ← unified config access
│  HaskellContext: toolchain, env,    │
│  paths, flags, src_root             │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Support Libraries (private/)       │
│  dependencies.bzl - dep graph merge │ ← helper modules
│  packages.bzl     - package exposure│
│  plugins.bzl      - compiler plugins│
│  pkg_id.bzl       - package IDs     │
│  expansions.bzl   - make variables  │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Actions (private/actions/)         │
│  compile.bzl      - GHC invocation  │ ← actual Bazel actions
│  link.bzl         - linking         │
│  package.bzl      - ghc-pkg recache │
│  info.bzl         - IDE output groups│
│  process_hsc.bzl  - hsc2hs          │
│  runghc.bzl       - runghc scripts  │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Providers (providers.bzl)          │
│  HaskellInfo, HaskellLibraryInfo,   │ ← info passed between rules
│  HaddockInfo, HaskellCoverageInfo,  │
│  etc. (12 total providers)          │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Toolchain (toolchain.bzl)          │
│  GHC location, flags, locale,       │ ← platform-specific GHC
│  global pkg-db, all tool binaries   │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Entry Points

### `haskell/defs.bzl` — Public API

Defines `_haskell_common_attrs` (shared attributes: `srcs`, `deps`, `ghcopts`,
`plugins`, etc.) and exposes the following public macros and rules:

| Name                        | Purpose                                      |
|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `haskell_library()`         | Build a Haskell library                      |
| `haskell_binary()`          | Build a Haskell executable                   |
| `haskell_test()`            | Build and run a Haskell test (with coverage) |
| `haskell_import`            | Import a prebuilt GHC package                |
| `haskell_toolchain_library` | Import a toolchain-supplied library          |
| `haskell_doc()`             | Generate Haddock documentation               |
| `haskell_repl()`            | Create GHCi REPL targets                     |
| `ghc_plugin()`              | Register a GHC compiler plugin               |
| `haskell_runfiles()`        | Runfiles-aware library wrapper               |

Every `haskell_library`, `haskell_binary`, and `haskell_test` macro
auto-generates a `@repl` target for interactive use.

### `haskell/providers.bzl` — Inter-rule Communication

| Provider                     | Content                                                       |
|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| `HaskellInfo`                | `package_databases`, `source_files`, `module_names`, `hs_libraries`, `interface_dirs`, `compile_flags`, per-module interface/object tracking |
| `HaskellLibraryInfo`         | `package_id`, `version`, `exports` (list of reexported pkg IDs) |
| `HaskellCabalArgsInfo`       | Cabal settings: `is_empty`, `ignore_setup`, `static_binary`, `with_haddock` |
| `HaskellToolchainLibraryInfo`| Marker for toolchain-imported libraries                       |
| `HaskellCoverageInfo`        | Code coverage data                                            |
| `HaddockInfo`                | `package_id`, `transitive_html`, `transitive_haddocks`        |
| `HaskellLintInfo`            | Linter output files                                           |
| `HaskellProtobufInfo`        | Protobuf-generated library info                               |
| `C2hsLibraryInfo`            | c2hs interface file and import dir                            |
| `GhcPluginInfo`              | Plugin module, deps, args, and tools                          |
| `HaskellCcLibrariesInfo`     | Maps C library keys to `HaskellCcLibraryInfo`                 |
| `HaskellCcLibraryInfo`       | Mangled static library links, `is_haskell` flag               |

## Implementation

### `haskell/private/haskell_impl.bzl` — Core Logic

Contains the implementation functions for every rule type:

- `haskell_library_impl` — compile modules, create package database via `ghc-pkg recache`
- `haskell_binary_impl` / `haskell_test_impl` — thin wrappers around `_haskell_binary_common_impl`
- `haskell_import_impl` — re-expose a prebuilt GHC package as a Bazel target
- `haskell_toolchain_library_impl` — import a toolchain-provided library

Key architectural note: **Empty Libraries** — fictitious packages without real
library files are used for module-level compilation to avoid cascading
rebuilds when only one module changes.

### `haskell/private/context.bzl` — HaskellContext

Creates the central `HaskellContext` struct/provder that carries:
- Toolchain reference (`@rules_haskell//haskell:toolchain`)
- Source root (workspace root + package + strip prefix)
- Environment variables (`LANG`, `RULES_HASKELL_GHC_PATH`, etc.)
- Coverage, worker, and compilation mode flags

### `haskell/private/dependencies.bzl` — Dependency Graph Merge

`gather_dep_info()` collapses all transitive `HaskellInfo` providers into a
single merged struct — the central dependency resolution point:
- Merges `package_databases`, `hs_libraries`, `interface_dirs`, `source_files`, `boot_files`
- Computes `package_ids` from `HaskellLibraryInfo` exports

## Actions (`haskell/private/actions/`)

| File                | Purpose                                       |
|---------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| `compile.bzl`       | GHC compilation (binary and library modes); handles `.hsc` preprocessing |
| `link.bzl`          | Linking executables and shared/static libraries |
| `package.bzl`       | Creates GHC package databases via `ghc-pkg recache` |
| `info.bzl`          | Output groups with interface files, objects, and package caches for IDE tooling |
| `process_hsc_file.bzl` | Run `hsc2hs` to convert `.hsc` files to `.hs` |
| `runghc.bzl`        | Generate runghc wrapper scripts with package exposure flags |

## Toolchain (`haskell/toolchain.bzl`)

Defines the `_haskell_toolchain` rule. The toolchain implementation:

1. Looks up `GHC_BINARIES` (`ghc`, `ghc-pkg`, `hsc2hs`, `haddock`, `runghc`, `hpc`)
2. Infers `libdir_path` and `docdir_path`
3. Dumps the global package database via `ghc-pkg dump --global`
4. Builds a `ToolchainInfo` provider containing:

| Field       | Content                                                  |
|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| `tools`     | Paths to GHC, ghc-pkg, hsc2hs, haddock, runghc, hpc, ar |
| `libraries` | Resolved toolchain library targets                       |
| `actions`   | Struct binding `compile_binary`, `compile_library`, `link_binary`, `link_library_dynamic`, `link_library_static`, `package`, `run_ghc` |
| `flags`     | GHC compiler flags                                       |
| `locale`    | `LANG` and locale archive                                |
| `is_darwin` / `cc_wrapper` etc. | Platform-specific info                        |
| `version`   | GHC version                                              |
| `global_pkg_db` | Path to the global package database dump             |
| `protoc`    | Protocol buffer compiler (if configured)                 |

### `_run_ghc()` — Central GHC Invocation

The toolchain's `_run_ghc()` function is the central bottleneck for all GHC
invocations. It handles:
- Persistent worker mode vs. direct invocation
- CC toolchain arguments (passes CC compiler flags to GHC)
- ABI hash extraction
- Locale setup (UTF-8 on macOS, fallback to `C.UTF-8`)
- Output cleaning (GHC outputs to stdout/stderr interleaved with worker protocol)

## Key Design Patterns

### 1. Worker-based Compilation

All rules delegate to a persistent GHC worker via `_haskell_worker_wrapper()`
(`defs.bzl`). The toolchain multiplexes through `_run_ghc()` which can either
maintain a persistent worker or run GHC directly. This amortizes GHC startup
cost across many small compilation units.

### 2. Aspect-driven Dependency Traversal

Three aspects propagate through the dependency graph collecting information
from transitive deps:

| Aspect                          | Purpose                                    |
|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `haskell_cc_libraries_aspect`   | Collect C/C++ library dependencies         |
| `haskell_doc_aspect`            | Gather transitive haddock docs             |
| `haskell_repl_aspect`           | Assemble REPL source files and packages    |

Using aspects avoids repeated work in action functions since Bazel applies them
once across the dep graph.

### 3. Platform Abstraction (`haskell/platforms/list.bzl`)

Maps diverse OS/arch name conventions onto canonical Bazel platform labels:

```
OS   → linux, osx (darwin), windows (mingw32), freebsd, ios, android
ARCH → x86_64, aarch64, arm, x86_32, ppc
```

`declare_config_settings()` generates `config_setting` rules per OS/arch, and
`platform_of_constraints()` combines them into strings like `"linux_x86_64"`.

### 4. Stackage Integration (`haskell/cabal.bzl`, ~2900 lines)

The `stack_snapshot()` repository rule converts Stackage snapshot YAML into
Bazel targets. Features:
- Per-GHC-version snapshot files (`stackage_snapshot_9.4.8.yaml`, etc.)
- Vendored packages (e.g. custom `ghc-paths` replacement)
- Custom setup dependencies
- `--with-PROG=PATH` flag injection for `alex`, `c2hs`, `cpphs`, `doctest`, `happy`
- `.netrc`-based authentication for private package downloads

### 5. CC Interop (`haskell/cc.bzl`, `haskell/private/cc_libraries.bzl`)

Bridges GHC's C compiler calling conventions with Bazel's CC toolchain:
- The `haskell_cc_libraries_aspect` collects transitive CC library deps
- `HaskellCcLibraryInfo` / `HaskellCcLibrariesInfo` providers carry the data
- macOS workarounds: `-u symbol` flags to prevent `-dead_strip_dylibs` from
  stripping indirectly-linked symbols (`link.bzl`)

### 6. Cabal Library Support (`haskell/cabal.bzl`)

Beyond `stack_snapshot`, the workspace-level Cabal integration:
- `_prepare_cabal_inputs()` sets up the full dependency tree as input files
- `_cabal_toolchain_info()` constructs a struct with paths to `ghc`, `ghc-pkg`,
  `hsc2hs`, `ar`, `cc`, `ld`
- Recognized Cabal configure flags are mapped to Bazel targets automatically

### 7. Build Configuration Profiles (`.bazelrc.common`)

| Config             | OS      | Toolchain Source  | Tag Filters                                    |
|--------------------|---------|-------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| `linux-nixpkgs`    | Linux   | Nixpkgs           | `-requires_nix`, `-dont_test_with_bindist`     |
| `macos-nixpkgs`    | macOS   | Nixpkgs           |                                                 |
| `linux-bindist`    | Linux   | GHC bindist       | `-requires_nix`, `-dont_test_with_bindist`     |
| `macos-bindist`    | macOS   | GHC bindist       | `-dont_test_on_darwin`                         |
| `windows-bindist`  | Windows | GHC bindist       | `-dont_test_on_windows`                        |
| `ci`               | any     | var.              | remote cache, w/ `CI=true`                     |

Coverage builds filter to `coverage-compatible` tagged tests only.

## Provider Flow

```
haskell_library → haskell_library_impl
  ├─ reads HaskellLibraryInfo + HaskellInfo from deps
  ├─ compiler compiles → produces .hi/.o files
  ├─ package.bzl creates package DB via ghc-pkg recache
  └─ emits HaskellLibraryInfo (package_id, version, exports)
       + HaskellInfo (source_files, package_databases, interface_dirs, ...)

haskell_binary → haskell_binary_impl
  ├─ merges all transitive dependency info
  ├─ compile_binary → .o files
  ├─ link_binary → executable
  └─ emits HaskellBinaryInfo + runfiles

haskell_import → haskell_import_impl
  └─ wraps a prebuilt GHC package as a Bazel target
```

